# Kanakko reminder jobs — installed to /etc/cron.d/kanakko, read by the `cron`
# daemon in the sidecar. DECISIONS §12 (the three jobs) and §10 (Asia/Kolkata).
#
# Times are Asia/Kolkata: the cron service sets TZ=Asia/Kolkata
# (docker-compose.yml) and tzdata is in the image, so the daemon reads these
# wall-clock times as IST. With TZ unset or unresolved they would fire in UTC —
# 5.5 hours early — with nothing logged about it (see tests/test_compose.py).
#
# cron strips the environment, so each line sources /app/cron.env (written from
# the container env by cron/entrypoint.sh) to get DATABASE_URL and
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN. Output goes to PID 1 (cron)'s stdout so each job's one log
# line — its only evidence of having run — reaches the container log.
#
# /etc/cron.d format carries a user field (root) between schedule and command;
# omit it and cron logs an error and ignores the whole file.

# m  h dom mon dow  user  command
0 12 * * *  root  . /app/cron.env; cd /app && /app/.venv/bin/python -m kanakko.jobs.noon    > /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
0 21 * * *  root  . /app/cron.env; cd /app && /app/.venv/bin/python -m kanakko.jobs.evening > /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
0 9 1 * *   root  . /app/cron.env; cd /app && /app/.venv/bin/python -m kanakko.jobs.monthly > /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
